WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.211
Little Fox readers.

2
00:00:13.991 --> 00:00:15.733
It's me, Alex, again.

3
00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:21.657
I took a trip to New York City with my family recently, and we went to the top

4
00:00:21.697 --> 00:00:23.459
of the Empire State building.

5
00:00:24.319 --> 00:00:29.944
When it was built more than 75 years ago, it was the tallest building in the world.

6
00:00:30.888 --> 00:00:31.488
But Mr.

7
00:00:31.568 --> 00:00:38.151
Fay just told us about another cool skyscraper—one that's more than twice that tall.

8
00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.493
It's the Burj Khalifa, located in Dubai.

9
00:00:43.374 --> 00:00:48.936
And as of 2010, it was the tallest building in the whole world!

10
00:00:50.457 --> 00:00:56.040
Dubai is a city in the United Arab Emirates, a small country on the Persian Gulf in the

11
00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:56.680
Middle East.

12
00:00:57.808 --> 00:01:02.632
Years ago people went to Dubai mainly to fish or dive for pearls.

13
00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:10.157
But after oil was discovered there in 1966, the city had a massive construction boom.

14
00:01:11.058 --> 00:01:19.844
And now it's a bustling world financial center, with tourists flocking to its upscale restaurants, stores, and hotels.

15
00:01:20.832 --> 00:01:28.156
Dubai also has some amazing sights, like man-made islands shaped like a map of the world and a

16
00:01:28.216 --> 00:01:30.357
ski resort that's indoors.

17
00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:32.398
Plus, Mr.

18
00:01:32.478 --> 00:01:40.321
Fay said there are plans to construct even more unique buildings, including a skyscraper with rotating floors and

19
00:01:40.381 --> 00:01:43.003
the world's first underwater hotel.

20
00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.484
I'd sure like to stay there!

21
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:52.525
But for now the Burj Khalifa is one of the most impressive buildings in Dubai.

22
00:01:53.426 --> 00:01:59.671
It was designed by Adrian Smith, a well-known architect, and an engineer named William F.

23
00:01:59.731 --> 00:02:07.197
Baker. They wanted the building to reflect modern architecture as well as the region's natural beauty.

24
00:02:08.218 --> 00:02:15.624
So to represent the Hymenocallis, a local flower, there are three wings arranged around a central core.

25
00:02:16.552 --> 00:02:21.934
The wings are set at different heights and appear to spiral around the building.

26
00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:27.375
This unique design makes for fantastic views of the Persian Gulf.

27
00:02:28.335 --> 00:02:35.578
More importantly, it helps to reduce the effects of Dubai's strong desert winds, which can reach speeds of

28
00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:38.178
fifty kilometers per hour near the ground.

29
00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:43.880
And at the top of the building, the wind can be about three times that strong!

30
00:02:45.348 --> 00:02:52.731
Since Dubai sits on a geological fault line, the building's designers faced another challenge: they had to make

31
00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:55.632
the tower strong enough to withstand earthquakes.

32
00:02:56.673 --> 00:03:01.475
That's why the building's three sections are buttressed by special concrete walls.

33
00:03:02.475 --> 00:03:09.098
These walls, along with the enormous concrete column in the center of the tower, make the building very

34
00:03:09.218 --> 00:03:11.739
sturdy. Oh, and Mr.

35
00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:14.000
Fay told us something really surprising.

36
00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:22.286
Since cities sometimes try to outdo each other by building taller and taller skyscrapers, the developers of the

37
00:03:22.346 --> 00:03:26.930
Burj Khalifa decided to keep their tower's final height a secret.

38
00:03:27.931 --> 00:03:33.275
But while they were building it, everyone could see that it was going to be one very tall

39
00:03:33.315 --> 00:03:38.360
building. The construction of the Burj Khalifa took about six years.

40
00:03:39.276 --> 00:03:45.780
During the peak of construction, there were more than twelve thousand workers at the site every single day!

41
00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:54.484
The building officially opened in January 2010 with a huge celebration and a massive fireworks display.

42
00:03:55.425 --> 00:04:05.430
At the grand opening, the builders finally revealed the exact height of the giant silver tower—828 meters—making it

43
00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.472
the tallest freestanding structure in the world.

44
00:04:09.428 --> 00:04:13.310
We learned some other really cool facts about the Burj Khalifa from Mr.

45
00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:23.856
Fay. It has 57 elevators, 8 escalators, and about 160 floors that are used as offices and apartments.

46
00:04:24.857 --> 00:04:31.961
There's also a really fancy restaurant and an expensive hotel that was designed by a famous fashion designer.

47
00:04:33.181 --> 00:04:35.583
The building also has about 28,000 glass panels.

48
00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.200
When I asked Mr.

49
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:46.063
Fay how they get washed, he explained that workers have to be harnessed into special mechanical units that

50
00:04:46.143 --> 00:04:48.464
extend out from the sides of the building.

51
00:04:49.385 --> 00:04:53.666
It takes three to four months to clean all that glass.

52
00:04:54.547 --> 00:04:57.428
Can you imagine washing windows up that high?

53
00:04:58.368 --> 00:05:00.289
I get dizzy just thinking about it!

54
00:05:01.129 --> 00:05:07.472
Speaking of heights, on the 124th floor of the Burj Khalifa, there's an observation deck.

55
00:05:08.272 --> 00:05:16.198
It's called At the Top, and it has floor-to-ceiling windows with amazing views of the city, the surrounding

56
00:05:16.258 --> 00:05:18.219
desert, and the Persian Gulf.

57
00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:25.164
And if you're feeling brave while you're up that high, you can check out the world's highest outdoor

58
00:05:25.384 --> 00:05:26.465
observation deck.

59
00:05:26.805 --> 00:05:29.367
Yikes! Mr.

60
00:05:29.427 --> 00:05:33.850
Fay told us that the world's tallest building isn't the only thing to see in the area.

61
00:05:34.711 --> 00:05:41.431
The Dubai Mall is nearby, and since this is Dubai we're talking about, the mall isn't just big;

62
00:05:41.971 --> 00:05:44.912
it's the biggest mall in the whole world.

63
00:05:45.913 --> 00:05:53.977
In addition to plenty of expensive stores, it has an aquarium, an Olympic-sized ice rink, and an indoor

64
00:05:54.037 --> 00:05:55.018
amusement park.

65
00:05:56.038 --> 00:05:59.280
The mall is also where you start your trip to At the Top.

66
00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:06.746
A moving walkway transports you from the mall to the high-speed elevators inside the Burj Khalifa.

67
00:06:08.147 --> 00:06:11.570
Lots of people also enjoy spending time at the park nearby.

68
00:06:12.391 --> 00:06:20.878
There's a lake, a promenade, a small forest, and a huge fountain with 1,500 jets that spray water

69
00:06:21.018 --> 00:06:21.839
over 150 meters high.

70
00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:32.864
With music, fog machines, and over six thousand lights, this famous "performing fountain" puts on quite a show!

71
00:06:33.824 --> 00:06:35.865
After the landmarks lesson, Mr.

72
00:06:35.945 --> 00:06:41.587
Fay gave our class a special assignment: we had to work with a partner and design our own

73
00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:45.949
skyscraper. Jake and I had lots of fun making ours.

74
00:06:46.929 --> 00:06:53.592
We used cardboard and covered it with aluminum foil to make our building shiny, like the Burj Khalifa.

75
00:06:54.564 --> 00:07:01.147
But we decided to put only one thing inside our tall tower—a gigantic water slide!

76
00:07:02.147 --> 00:07:02.907
Awesome, huh?
